{"access":"public","aliases":[],"assertions":[{"claim_ids":["clm_18af7774347af85d50b9bdc14bc93ac2c2fc8671748934cc8b26dcbb3cb0c947"],"opposing_claim_ids":[],"text":"Editor plugins for Vim, VSCode, IntelliJ, and Sublime Text are listed as clients that interact with the app."},{"claim_ids":["clm_3ba16f52d426518000b1cda2bc4afd53a35cdc110f53f9e6e0b2d4129bdcd897"],"opposing_claim_ids":[],"text":"Editor plugins POST highlighted code to a blueprints#create endpoint, and highlighted descriptions to blueprint_variants#create."},{"claim_ids":["clm_40117f1a9f326954dda82be8ee636fcc6162264eb45f097f3c5c120418b3bf67"],"opposing_claim_ids":[],"text":"The project is a Ruby on Rails application for storing code chunks called 'blueprints' and using them as a base for GPT-4 to generate new code."},{"claim_ids":["clm_4b28b9ef37e2ad618a2c639b3fda66713de6ae646d2557414ee78612608f63eb"],"opposing_claim_ids":[],"text":"Blueprint variant creation finds the closest blueprint by description, sends its description and code plus the new description to GPT-4, and replaces the highlighted editor text with the result."},{"claim_ids":["clm_77a57a3ab8e860518ef47f4e491f777294aec9ec2a8d85f95b0d2afaebacd4d8"],"opposing_claim_ids":[],"text":"The app serves a web UI at http://localhost:3000 where users can view stored blueprints and their descriptions."},{"claim_ids":["clm_82d7d805eeba38c335ad3a4040107f7e48be13cc083398b913dac6628326a2d2"],"opposing_claim_ids":[],"text":"An alternative Google Gemini provider is supported by setting GEMINI_API_KEY and changing config.ai_provider to 'google' in config/application.rb."},{"claim_ids":["clm_887dfdec9d68c7dab2c3ca3bf61cdb9c14b68215f6b654518a128c6cda9d2800"],"opposing_claim_ids":[],"text":"Creating a blueprint sends code to GPT-4 to generate a name and description, then stores vector embeddings of the description with the record in the database."},{"claim_ids":["clm_a2c657e34463e112e2d899cf21cfd8a429c60ee04b3d4c1db740c7a7d92f3f8c"],"opposing_claim_ids":[],"text":"The app depends on Postgres with pgvector (installed via Homebrew per setup instructions) and requires an OpenAI API key in the OPENAI_API_KEY environment variable."},{"claim_ids":["clm_c6183f3d9e109d122b688d2e3aaca069360baee6cc1d7e6bf11d550d38bd2700"],"opposing_claim_ids":[],"text":"Repository development practice: setup involves cloning the repo, running bundle install, creating and migrating the database with bin/rails commands, building Tailwind CSS, and starting the server with bin/rails s."},{"claim_ids":["clm_ef1f24be1034960b57022095cb5a652ae3a929193d5ac4fcb1e7371eddbdb762"],"opposing_claim_ids":[],"text":"Repository development practice: LLM performance specs are run by listing models in spec_perforamnce/llms/ai_models.yml and running 'rspec spec_performance', with appropriate LLM setup required per the sublayer repo."},{"claim_ids":["clm_fc58ecdd732395b6a10e84e3ad8277f318498510794379f6b8a9a3a07d910427"],"opposing_claim_ids":[],"text":"The project targets developers using LLMs for code generation, with a demo video and blog post provided, and invites community participation via the Sublayer Discord."}],"claim_ids":["clm_18af7774347af85d50b9bdc14bc93ac2c2fc8671748934cc8b26dcbb3cb0c947","clm_3ba16f52d426518000b1cda2bc4afd53a35cdc110f53f9e6e0b2d4129bdcd897","clm_40117f1a9f326954dda82be8ee636fcc6162264eb45f097f3c5c120418b3bf67","clm_4b28b9ef37e2ad618a2c639b3fda66713de6ae646d2557414ee78612608f63eb","clm_77a57a3ab8e860518ef47f4e491f777294aec9ec2a8d85f95b0d2afaebacd4d8","clm_82d7d805eeba38c335ad3a4040107f7e48be13cc083398b913dac6628326a2d2","clm_887dfdec9d68c7dab2c3ca3bf61cdb9c14b68215f6b654518a128c6cda9d2800","clm_a2c657e34463e112e2d899cf21cfd8a429c60ee04b3d4c1db740c7a7d92f3f8c","clm_c6183f3d9e109d122b688d2e3aaca069360baee6cc1d7e6bf11d550d38bd2700","clm_ef1f24be1034960b57022095cb5a652ae3a929193d5ac4fcb1e7371eddbdb762","clm_fc58ecdd732395b6a10e84e3ad8277f318498510794379f6b8a9a3a07d910427"],"created_at":"2026-09-14T04:24:21Z","created_by_operation":"op_0721e4a140f549c